# EsFlowerSway — a C++ script CLASS, not a script file.
#
# THE RUNTIME NEVER READS THESE BYTES.  A .jcecpp path NAMES a class published
# by a compiled module; cpp_instantiate strips the directory and the extension
# and looks the name up in the module registry.  The class is in
# src/es_flower_sway.cpp, built into elemental_serenity.exe and into
# es_scripts.dll (which the editor loads — see jce_project.json).
#
# THIS FILE EXISTS SO THE OFFLINE HALF OF THE PIPELINE CAN SEE IT.  The
# editor's asset database, the Script component's picker, the cooker and the
# publication policy all classify by extension through the one catalog in
# engine/src/resource/jce_asset_ext.c, and they classify FILES.  With this
# stub the script is attachable by picking it like any other; without it the
# path still works and has to be typed by hand.  Its form in the catalog is
# REFERENCE, so the archive cooker does not put it in the shared text
# dictionary the way it would a real source file.
